JobBridge Nepal: Next.js Modular Development Guide
📁 Project Structure & Naming Conventions
⚠️ Critical Rule: All Names in Lowercase Kebab-Case
ALL file and folder names must be lowercase kebab-case (e.g., job-card.component.tsx). No PascalCase or camelCase for file names.

File Naming Pattern
Format: name.type.ts or name.type.tsx

job-list.component.tsx (UI)

use-application-status.hook.ts (Logic)

contract-generator.service.ts (Business logic/API)

auth.middleware.ts (Next.js Middleware)

Folder Naming Pattern
Singular for feature modules: job-management/, contract-signing/

Plural for shared collections: components/, hooks/, services/

🏗️ Modular Architecture (Domain-Driven)
The project is organized by Feature Modules. Each module is self-contained, representing a core objective of JobBridge Nepal.

src/
├── app/                   # Next.js App Router (Routes & Layouts)
│   ├── (auth)/            # Grouped auth routes
│   ├── (dashboard)/       # Grouped protected routes
│   │   ├── jobs/          # Job browsing & management
│   │   └── contracts/     # Digital NDA/Contract routes
│   └── api/               # Route Handlers (Backend logic)
│
├── modules/               # Core Feature Modules
│   ├── ai-recommendation/ # KNN-based matching logic 
│   ├── application-tracking/ # Multi-stage status updates [cite: 33]
│   ├── contract-management/ # E-signature & NDA logic [cite: 36]
│   └── messaging/         # Stage-based communication [cite: 38]
│
├── components/            # Shared UI (Buttons, Inputs, Modals)
├── core/                  # Global configs, axios instances, constants
└── lib/                   # External library wrappers (e.g., ml-knn) 
🛠️ Core Technology Stack
Framework: Next.js 15+ (App Router)

Language: TypeScript


Backend: Node.js (via Next.js Route Handlers) 


AI Engine: ml-knn for personalized suggestions 



Styling: Tailwind CSS (Mobile-responsive for Nepal's market) 


State Management: React Query (Server state), Zustand/Redux (Client state)


Security: RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) 

📑 Feature Module Standards
1. Application Tracking System (ATS) 

Each stage update must trigger a notification.

File: modules/application-tracking/services/tracking.service.ts

Logic: Use a state machine to move applicants from "Applied" to "Interview" to "Hired/Rejected".

2. AI Recommendation Module 



Implementation: Integrate ml-knn within the Node.js backend environment.

Naming: modules/ai-recommendation/utils/knn-engine.utils.ts


Requirement: Fallback to rule-based filtering if dataset is too small.

3. Digital Contract & NDA 


Implementation: Secure creation and signing of employment agreements.


Safety: Platform facilitates signatures but does not provide legal enforcement.

Folder: modules/contract-management/components/signature-pad.component.tsx

📐 Development Guidelines
1. File Size & Responsibility
Limit: Max 500 lines per file.

Extraction: If a job listing component grows too large, extract job-details.component.tsx and application-form.component.tsx.

2. Server vs. Client Components
Server Components: Use for data fetching (Job listings, Profile data).

Client Components: Use for interactive forms, signature pads, and real-time messaging tabs.

3. Error & Loading States

Requirement: Every feature must include a loading.tsx and error.tsx in its respective app/ directory to ensure smooth UX for mobile-first users in Nepal.


🎨 Design & Color Management
Following the Apple + Financial Excellence style from your guide:

Primary: #007AFF (Apple Blue) for action buttons.

Status Colors:

Success: Green for "Hired" or "Signed".

Warning: Orange for "Interview Scheduled".

Danger: Red for "Rejected" or "Dissolved".

CSS Variables: Use var(--primary-text) and var(--background-color) to support Dark/Light mode.

🚀 Deployment & Roadmap

Methodology: Waterfall Prototype Model.


Timeline: 12 Weeks total.


Current Goal: Complete Phase 1 (Requirement Analysis) and Phase 2 (System Design).
